$DIR/main.p:14:24: b was moved into consume (its parameter takes a Buf by value) at line 14 in the previous iteration of this loop
    Buf is an owner type: its values own what they hold and release it when they
    are dropped. b is declared outside the loop, and the loop moves its value
    away at line 14 without giving it a new one, so when the next iteration
    starts b holds nothing.
    Go copies such values freely and its garbage collector frees what they refer
    to when nothing refers to it any more. Plutonium has no garbage collector:
    an owner frees what it owns when it is dropped, so there must be exactly
    one.
    Declare b inside the loop, so that each iteration has its own:
        for ... {
            var b Buf
            ...
        }
    Or give b a new value after line 14:
        b = Buf{}
    (see "Moves" in the Plutonium spec, section 18.5)
    (run "pluto explain E3302" for a longer explanation)

